(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the biogeochemical Nitrogen Cycle in marine and terrestrial ecosystems, evaluating anthropogenic Haber-Bosch inputs and eutrophication.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Biogeochemical Nitrogen Cycle and Anthropogenic Nitrogen Perturbations:) Tj
T*
(   1. Fundamental Natural Nitrogen Cycle:) Tj
T*
(   Atmospheric dinitrogen \(N2\) comprises 78% of the atmosphere, held by a strong triple covalent) Tj
T*
(   bond \(N#N, dissociation energy = 945 kJ/mol\) that cannot be assimilated by plants without) Tj
T*
(   reduction:) Tj
T*
(   - Biological Nitrogen Fixation \(BNF\): Natural terrestrial fixation by symbiotic and free-living) Tj
T*
(   prokaryotes generates ~100 to 140 Tg N/year.) Tj
T*
(   - Assimilation & Ammonification: Plants absorb NH4+ and NO3- to synthesize proteins and nucleic) Tj
T*
(   acids. Decomposers mineralize organic nitrogen back into ammonia \(ammonification\).) Tj
T*
(   - Nitrification & Denitrification: Aerobic nitrifiers convert ammonia to nitrate; anaerobic) Tj
T*
(   denitrifiers reduce nitrate back to N2 and N2O gases, closing the cycle.) Tj
T*
(   2. The Anthropogenic Revolution: The Haber-Bosch Process:) Tj
T*
