T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the Ghyben-Herzberg Principle governing coastal aquifer freshwater-seawater equilibrium, and evaluate artificial recharge engineering.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Coastal Aquifer Salinization, the Ghyben-Herzberg Equilibrium, and Barrier Engineering:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Ghyben-Herzberg Hydrostatic Principle:) Tj
T*
(   - In coastal aquifers, freshwater originating from precipitation floats as a lens on top of) Tj
T*
(   heavier, denser saline seawater:) Tj
T*
(   * Freshwater density: rho_f = 1.000 g/cm3.) Tj
T*
(   * Seawater density: rho_s = 1.025 g/cm3.) Tj
T*
(   - At hydrostatic equilibrium along the subterranean freshwater-saltwater interface:) Tj
T*
(   rho_s * g * z = rho_f * g * \(h + z\)) Tj
T*
(   Where h is the freshwater water table elevation above mean sea level, and z is the depth of the) Tj
T*
(   saltwater interface below mean sea level.) Tj
T*
(   - Rearranging:) Tj
T*
(   z = [ rho_f / \(rho_s - rho_f\) ] * h = [ 1.000 / \(1.025 - 1.000\) ] * h = 40 * h) Tj
T*
(   - Significance: For every 1 meter of freshwater head above sea level, there exists a column of) Tj
T*
(   40 meters of freshwater extending below sea level.) Tj
T*
(   2. Saltwater Upconing Induced by Over-Extraction:) Tj
T*
(   If excessive municipal or agricultural pumping lowers the freshwater water table by just 1.0) Tj
T*
(   meter \(Delta h = -1.0 m\), the Ghyben-Herzberg relation dictates that the underlying saltwater) Tj
T*
(   interface will rise vertically by 40 meters \(Delta z = +40 m\)! This phenomenon \('upconing'\)) Tj
T*
(   salinizes production wells, rendering groundwater non-potable and unfit for agriculture.) Tj
T*
(   3. Coastal Engineering Mitigation Strategies:) Tj
T*
(   - Artificial Aquifer Recharge: Injecting treated reclaimed wastewater or surplus monsoon storm) Tj
T*
(   runoff into infiltration basins or direct injection wells to artificially maintain freshwater) Tj
T*
(   hydraulic head \(h\).) Tj
T*
(   - Subsurface Hydraulic Seawater Intrusion Barriers: Pumping desalinated or recycled water into) Tj
T*
(   a linear array of coastal injection wells to maintain an artificial hydrodynamic ridge that) Tj
T*
(   repels incoming saltwater wedges.) Tj
T*
