(   [Problem Statement]: Evaluate the thermodynamics of Fossil Fuel Combustion, formulate the stoichiometric air-fuel ratio, and analyze the concept of Energy Return on Investment \(EROI\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Fossil Fuel Combustion Geochemistry, Stoichiometry, and EROI Dynamics:) Tj
T*
(   1. Thermochemical Combustion Stoichiometry:) Tj
T*
(   Fossil fuels \(coal, petroleum, natural gas\) store chemical potential energy in covalent C-C and) Tj
T*
(   C-H bonds formed over hundreds of millions of years.) Tj
T*
(   - Ideal Methane Combustion:) Tj
T*
(   CH4 \(g\) + 2 O2 \(g\) -> CO2 \(g\) + 2 H2O \(l\) + Delta H_combustion \(-891 kJ/mol\)) Tj
T*
(   - High Heating Value \(HHV\) vs Low Heating Value \(LHV\):) Tj
T*
(   * HHV \(Gross Calorific Value\): Includes the latent heat of vaporization recovered by condensing) Tj
T*
(   exhaust water vapor back to liquid at 25 deg C.) Tj
T*
(   * LHV \(Net Calorific Value\): Assumes exhaust water exits the chimney as hot steam \(vapor\),) Tj
T*
(   which is the realistic operational value for industrial boilers.) Tj
T*
(   2. Stoichiometric Air-to-Fuel Ratio:) Tj
T*
(   Air contains approximately 21% O2 and 79% N2 by volume \(3.76 moles N2 per mole O2\).) Tj
T*
(   For 1 mole of methane:) Tj
T*
(   CH4 + 2 \(O2 + 3.76 N2\) -> CO2 + 2 H2O + 7.52 N2) Tj
T*
(   - Stoichiometric Mass Air-Fuel Ratio \(AFR_stoic\):) Tj
T*
(   Mass Air / Mass Fuel = [ 2 * \(32 + 3.76 * 28\) ] / [ 16.04 ] = 274.56 / 16.04 = 17.11 kg air /) Tj
T*
(   kg methane.) Tj
T*
(   3. Energy Return on Investment \(EROI\):) Tj
T*
(   - Mathematical Formulation \(Charles Hall\):) Tj
T*
(   EROI = \(Total Gross Energy Delivered by a Resource\) / \(Total Energy Invested to Extract,) Tj
T*
(   Refine, and Deliver It\)) Tj
T*
(   - Historical Trajectory and The Energetic Cliff:) Tj
T*
(   In the 1930s, conventional oil extraction exhibited an EROI exceeding 100:1 \(investing 1 barrel) Tj
T*
(   yielded 100 barrels\). As sweet crude reserves deplete, exploration shifts to ultra-deep) Tj
T*
(   offshore, tar sands, and hydraulic fracturing, driving EROI down to 10:1 or 5:1.) Tj
T*
(   A modern technological civilization requires an average societal EROI of at least 8:1 to 10:1) Tj
T*
(   to support healthcare, education, transport, and science beyond basic survival.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
