(   [Problem Statement]: Compare Solar Photovoltaic \(PV\) semiconductor physics with Concentrated Solar Power \(CSP\) thermal engineering, including molten-salt storage.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Solar Energy Engineering: Photovoltaic Semiconductor Physics vs. Concentrated Solar Power:) Tj
T*
(   1. Solar Photovoltaic \(PV\) Physics:) Tj
T*
(   - Operating Principle: Relies on the Photovoltaic Effect in semiconductor P-N junctions) Tj
T*
(   \(silicon\).) Tj
T*
(   - Mechanism:) Tj
T*
(   * Doping: Crystalline silicon \(Group IV\) is doped with phosphorus \(Group V\) to form N-type) Tj
T*
(   \(free electrons\) and boron \(Group III\) to form P-type \(holes\).) Tj
T*
(   * P-N Junction: Diffusion of charge carriers across the interface creates an internal) Tj
T*
(   electrostatic depletion zone and built-in electric field \(E-field\).) Tj
T*
(   * Photo-generation: Incident solar photons with energy exceeding the silicon bandgap \(h*nu >) Tj
T*
(   E_g = 1.12 eV\) excite valence electrons into the conduction band, generating electron-hole) Tj
T*
(   pairs.) Tj
T*
(   * Charge Separation: The internal electric field sweeps electrons toward the N-contact and) Tj
T*
(   holes toward the P-contact, generating direct current \(DC\) electricity without moving parts.) Tj
T*
