(>> Solution to Question 15:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the theoretical Betz Limit for wind turbine rotor aerodynamic power efficiency, and explain wind power scaling laws.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Aerodynamics of Wind Turbines, Betz Limit Derivation, and Scaling Laws:) Tj
T*
(   1. Wind Stream Power Formulation:) Tj
T*
(   The mass flow rate of air \(density rho\) passing through a rotor disc of swept area A \(radius R,) Tj
T*
(   A = pi * R^2\) at undisturbed wind velocity v is:) Tj
T*
(   m_dot = rho * A * v) Tj
T*
(   The kinetic energy per unit mass is 0.5 * v^2. Thus, the total instantaneous kinetic power in) Tj
T*
(   the wind stream is:) Tj
T*
(   P_wind = 0.5 * m_dot * v^2 = 0.5 * rho * A * v^3) Tj
T*
(   Crucial Scaling: Power scales with the cube of wind velocity \(v^3\) and the square of rotor) Tj
T*
(   radius \(R^2\)! Doubling wind speed increases available power 8-fold.) Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Derivation of the Betz Limit \(Albert Betz, 1919\):) Tj
T*
(   - Let undisturbed upstream wind speed be v1, wind speed at the rotor plane be u, and downstream) Tj
T*
(   far-wake velocity be v2.) Tj
T*
(   - By conservation of linear momentum: Actuator disc theory states that u = 0.5 * \(v1 + v2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Thrust force on the rotor: T = m_dot * \(v1 - v2\) = rho * A * u * \(v1 - v2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Power extracted by the rotor: P = T * u = rho * A * u^2 * \(v1 - v2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Define the axial induction factor a such that u = v1 * \(1 - a\), hence v2 = v1 * \(1 - 2a\).) Tj
T*
(   - Power extracted becomes:) Tj
T*
(   P = 2 * rho * A * v1^3 * a * \(1 - a\)^2) Tj
T*
(   - Power Coefficient: C_p = P / P_wind = 4 * a * \(1 - a\)^2.) Tj
T*
(   - Maximizing C_p with respect to induction factor a:) Tj
T*
(   d\(C_p\)/da = 4 * [ \(1 - a\)^2 - 2a * \(1 - a\) ] = 4 * \(1 - a\) * \(1 - 3a\) = 0) Tj
T*
(   Yields optimal induction factor: a = 1/3.) Tj
T*
(   - Substituting a = 1/3 into C_p:) Tj
T*
(   C_p,max = 4 * \(1/3\) * \(1 - 1/3\)^2 = 4/3 * 4/9 = 16/27 approx 0.5926 \(59.3%\).) Tj
T*
(   - Conclusion: No physical wind turbine can convert more than 59.3% of the kinetic energy in) Tj
T*
(   wind into mechanical shaft power.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
