(   1. Hydropower Potential Formulation:) Tj
T*
(   The theoretical hydraulic power P available from falling water is:) Tj
T*
(   P = eta * rho * g * Q * H_net) Tj
T*
(   Where:) Tj
T*
(   - eta: Total electromechanical conversion efficiency \(turbine + alternator, typically 0.85 to) Tj
T*
(   0.92\).) Tj
T*
(   - rho: Water density \(1000 kg/m3\).) Tj
T*
(   - g: Gravitational acceleration \(9.81 m/s2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Q: Volumetric flow rate through penstocks \(m3/s\).) Tj
T*
(   - H_net: Net effective hydraulic head \(gross head minus friction head losses in tunnels and) Tj
T*
(   penstocks, m\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Hydraulic Turbine Classification:) Tj
T*
(   - Impulse Turbines \(Pelton Wheel\): Suitable for high head \(H > 250 m\) and low volumetric) Tj
T*
(   discharge. Water discharges through high-velocity nozzles into atmospheric buckets on the) Tj
T*
(   runner wheel.) Tj
T*
(   - Reaction Turbines:) Tj
T*
(   * Francis Turbine: Mixed-flow \(radial inlet, axial outlet\) turbine, ideal for medium heads \(30) Tj
T*
(   m to 300 m\) and medium flow rates. Most widely deployed global hydropower turbine.) Tj
T*
(   * Kaplan Turbine: Purely axial flow propeller turbine with adjustable runner blades and guide) Tj
T*
(   vanes, optimized for low head \(H < 30 m\) and very large volumetric discharge.) Tj
T*
(   3. Environmental and Ecological Impacts:) Tj
T*
(   - Upstream Inundation: Flooding of pristine terrestrial forests, fertile agricultural) Tj
T*
(   floodplains, and cultural displacement of indigenous riverine populations. Submerged) Tj
T*
(   decomposing vegetation releases substantial quantities of methane \(CH4\) under anoxic) Tj
T*
(   hypolimnetic conditions.) Tj
T*
(   - Downstream River Fragmentation: Concrete dam walls block migratory fish runs \(e.g., salmon,) Tj
T*
(   mahseer\), disrupting spawning cycles \(partially mitigated by fish ladders\).) Tj
T*
(   - Trapping of Fluvial Sediment: Dams trap 90% to 99% of gravel and mineral silt, causing) Tj
T*
(   downstream riverbed incision \('hungry water' erosion\) and coastal delta shrinkage.) Tj
T*
