(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the biochemical stages of Anaerobic Digestion for Biogas production, the stoichiometry of methanogenesis, and optimal operational parameters.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Biochemical Kinetics and Process Optimization of Anaerobic Biogas Digestion:) Tj
T*
(   1. Four Sequential Biochemical Stages:) Tj
T*
(   - Stage 1: Hydrolysis: Extracellular hydrolytic enzymes \(cellulases, proteases, lipases\)) Tj
T*
(   secreted by facultative bacteria cleave insoluble, complex polymers \(cellulose, starch,) Tj
T*
(   proteins, fats\) into soluble monomers \(glucose, amino acids, glycerol, fatty acids\). This is) Tj
T*
(   the rate-limiting step for lignocellulosic agricultural feedstocks.) Tj
T*
(   - Stage 2: Acidogenesis \(Fermentation\): Acidogenic bacteria metabolize monomers into) Tj
T*
(   short-chain Volatile Fatty Acids \(propionate, butyrate, valerate\), lactic acid, alcohols, CO2,) Tj
T*
(   and H2.) Tj
T*
(   - Stage 3: Acetogenesis: Obligate hydrogen-producing acetogenic bacteria \(OHPA\) oxidize higher) Tj
T*
(   VFAs into acetic acid \(CH3COOH\), CO2, and H2:) Tj
T*
(   CH3CH2COO- \(propionate\) + 2 H2O -> CH3COO- + 3 H2 + CO2) Tj
T*
(   Thermodynamically endergonic \(Delta G > 0\) unless syntrophic hydrogen-consuming methanogens) Tj
T*
(   continuously remove H2, keeping partial pressure P_H2 < 10^-4 bar.) Tj
T*
(   - Stage 4: Methanogenesis: Strictly anaerobic Archaea synthesize methane via two distinct) Tj
T*
(   metabolic pathways:) Tj
T*
(   * Acetoclastic Methanogenesis \(Methanosarcina, Methanosaeta, generating ~70% of total biogas\):) Tj
T*
(   CH3COOH -> CH4 + CO2 \(Delta G0' = -31 kJ/mol\)) Tj
T*
(   * Hydrogenotrophic Methanogenesis \(Methanobacterium, generating ~30% of biogas\):) Tj
T*
