(   [Problem Statement]: Formulate the chemical mechanism of Biodiesel Transesterification, contrast homogeneous and heterogeneous catalysts, and specify ASTM D6751 fuel standards.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Biodiesel Chemical Synthesis via Transesterification and Fuel Quality Standards:) Tj
T*
(   1. Chemical Mechanism of Transesterification:) Tj
T*
(   Vegetable oils and animal fats consist of triglycerides \(esters of glycerol and three) Tj
T*
(   long-chain fatty acids\). Transesterification is a three-step reversible catalytic reaction) Tj
T*
(   replacing glycerol with a low-molecular-weight alcohol \(methanol or ethanol\):) Tj
T*
(   - Stepwise Conversion:) Tj
T*
(   Triglyceride + CH3OH <-> Diglyceride + Fatty Acid Methyl Ester \(FAME\)) Tj
T*
(   Diglyceride + CH3OH <-> Monoglyceride + FAME) Tj
T*
(   Monoglyceride + CH3OH <-> Glycerol + FAME) Tj
T*
(   - Overall Stoichiometry:) Tj
T*
(   Triglyceride + 3 CH3OH --[Catalyst]--> 3 FAME \(Biodiesel\) + Glycerol) Tj
T*
(   - Stoichiometric ratio is 3:1 \(methanol to oil\), but an industrial molar ratio of 6:1 is) Tj
T*
(   employed to shift chemical equilibrium toward complete FAME conversion.) Tj
T*
(   2. Catalyst Comparison:) Tj
T*
(   - Homogeneous Alkaline Catalysts \(NaOH, KOH, Sodium methoxide CH3ONa\):) Tj
T*
(   * Advantages: Fast reaction kinetics \(30-60 min at 60 deg C\), high conversion \(> 98%\), operates) Tj
T*
(   under atmospheric pressure.) Tj
T*
(   * Limitations: Free Fatty Acids \(FFA > 1%\) react with base to form soaps \(saponification:) Tj
T*
(   R-COOH + KOH -> R-COOK + H2O\), causing severe phase emulsion and destroying yield.) Tj
T*
(   - Heterogeneous Solid Base/Acid Catalysts \(CaO, Mg-Al hydrotalcites, sulfated zirconia\):) Tj
T*
(   * Advantages: Easy mechanical catalyst recovery, eliminates wash water effluent, tolerates high) Tj
T*
(   FFA feedstocks.) Tj
T*
(   * Limitations: Mass transfer resistance, requires higher temperatures \(> 120-180 deg C\) and) Tj
T*
(   pressures, risk of catalyst deactivation by surface leaching.) Tj
T*
(   3. ASTM D6751 Fuel Specifications:) Tj
T*
(   - Kinematic Viscosity \(40 deg C\): 1.9 to 6.0 mm2/s \(critical to ensure proper fuel injector) Tj
T*
(   atomization\).) Tj
T*
(   - Flash Point: Minimum 93 deg C \(ensures fire safety during transport\).) Tj
T*
(   - Cetane Number: Minimum 47 \(governs ignition delay in diesel engines\).) Tj
T*
(   - Free and Total Glycerin: Maximum 0.020% and 0.240% by mass \(prevents injector fouling\).) Tj
T*
