(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the thermodynamic principles and engineering challenges of Ocean Thermal Energy Conversion \(OTEC\), and analyze Closed-Cycle vs Open-Cycle systems.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Ocean Thermal Energy Conversion \(OTEC\): Thermodynamic Cycle and Fluid Mechanics:) Tj
T*
(   1. Fundamental Thermodynamic Principle:) Tj
T*
(   The ocean acts as a gigantic natural solar thermal collector and storage system. Between the) Tj
T*
(   sun-warmed tropical surface layer \(0 to 50 m depth, T_surface = 25 to 28 deg C\) and the cold) Tj
T*
(   deep polar-origin waters \(800 to 1,000 m depth, T_deep = 4 to 6 deg C\), there exists a) Tj
T*
(   continuous, non-intermittent temperature differential: Delta T approx 20 to 22 deg C.) Tj
T*
(   2. Thermodynamic Limitations \(Carnot Efficiency\):) Tj
T*
(   Operating between T_hot = 299 K \(26 deg C\) and T_cold = 278 K \(5 deg C\), the theoretical) Tj
T*
(   maximum Carnot thermal efficiency is:) Tj
T*
(   eta_Carnot = 1 - \(T_cold / T_hot\) = 1 - \(278 / 299\) = 0.0702 \(7.02%\).) Tj
T*
(   Accounting for heat exchanger thermal approach pinches and pumping parasitic loads, actual net) Tj
T*
(   thermal efficiency is only 2.5% to 4.0%. Consequently, OTEC requires colossal volumetric flow) Tj
T*
(   rates of seawater to generate commercial megawatt-scale power.) Tj
T*
(   3. System Configurations:) Tj
T*
(   - Closed-Cycle OTEC \(Anderson Cycle\):) Tj
T*
(   Warm surface seawater pumps through an evaporator to vaporize a low-boiling working fluid \(pure) Tj
T*
(   anhydrous ammonia, NH3, boiling point -33.3 deg C at 1 atm\). High-pressure ammonia vapor) Tj
T*
(   expands through a low-pressure turbine driving a generator. Exhaust ammonia vapor is condensed) Tj
T*
(   back into liquid in a condenser cooled by cold deep seawater pumped through a 1,000-meter-long) Tj
T*
(   cold water pipe \(CWP\).) Tj
T*
(   - Open-Cycle OTEC \(Claude Cycle\):) Tj
T*
(   Warm surface seawater is directly flash-evaporated into steam inside a specialized vacuum) Tj
T*
(   chamber operated at 0.03 bar pressure \(where water boils at 24 deg C\). Low-pressure water vapor) Tj
T*
(   expands through an enormous low-density steam turbine. When condensed against cold deep) Tj
T*
(   seawater in a surface condenser, it yields desalinated freshwater as a coproduct.) Tj
T*
(   4. Key Engineering Challenges:) Tj
T*
(   - Cold Water Pipe \(CWP\) Structural Mechanics: Suspending a 4 to 10-meter-diameter fiberglass) Tj
T*
(   reinforced plastic \(FRP\) pipe down to 1,000 m depth in deep oceanic shear currents and) Tj
T*
(   hurricane waves.) Tj
T*
(   - Marine Biofouling: Rapid biological slime and macro-fouling \(barnacles, mussels\) coating heat) Tj
T*
(   exchanger plates, degrading thermal heat transfer coefficients.) Tj
T*
