(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Biophysical Mechanisms of Biomagnification and the Minamata Bay Methylmercury Case Study:) Tj
T*
(   1. Physicochemical Basis of Biomagnification:) Tj
T*
(   Biomagnification is governed by three physicochemical properties:) Tj
T*
(   - High Octanol-Water Partition Coefficient \(log K_ow > 4.5\): Hydrophobic, lipophilic pollutants) Tj
T*
(   partition out of aqueous solutions and dissolve selectively into biological adipose tissues and) Tj
T*
(   cellular lipid membranes.) Tj
T*
(   - Low Metabolic Clearance Rate: Resistant to endogenous enzymatic breakdown \(cytochrome P450) Tj
T*
(   monooxygenases\) due to halogenation \(DDT, PCBs\) or organometallic covalent bonds) Tj
T*
(   \(methylmercury\).) Tj
T*
(   - Low Excretion Rate: Bound tightly to tissue proteins or lipid depots, leading to biological) Tj
T*
(   half-lives of years to decades.) Tj
T*
(   2. Fugacity-Based Trophic Accumulation Mechanism:) Tj
T*
(   - When an organism ingests food, digestion digests lipids and proteins, reducing the total mass) Tj
T*
(   of the gut contents.) Tj
T*
(   - Because the persistent contaminant cannot be absorbed or broken down, its thermodynamic) Tj
T*
(   fugacity \(escaping chemical tendency\) increases in the gut lumen.) Tj
T*
(   - This creates a passive chemical gradient driving the contaminant across the intestinal) Tj
T*
(   epithelium into the organism's blood and somatic tissue.) Tj
T*
(   - With an assimilation efficiency of food of ~80% and a contaminant excretion rate near zero,) Tj
T*
(   the contaminant concentration increases by a biomagnification factor \(BMF = C_predator /) Tj
T*
(   C_prey\) of 2 to 10 at each consecutive trophic level.) Tj
T*
(   3. The Minamata Bay Methylmercury Disaster:) Tj
T*
(   - Industrial Source: Chisso Corporation's acetaldehyde chemical manufacturing facility) Tj
T*
(   discharged industrial wastewater containing methylmercury catalysts [CH3Hg+] into Minamata Bay,) Tj
T*
(   Japan \(1932 to 1968\).) Tj
T*
(   - Biogeochemical Transformation: Sulfate-reducing bacteria in anoxic estuarine sediment) Tj
T*
(   methylated inorganic mercury into lipophilic monomethylmercury:) Tj
T*
(   Hg2+ + Methylcobalamin \(Vitamin B12\) -> [CH3-Hg]+) Tj
T*
(   - Biomagnification Cascade: Seawater [Hg] \(~0.0001 ppm\) -> Phytoplankton \(0.01 ppm\) ->) Tj
T*
(   Zooplankton \(0.1 ppm\) -> Small Fish \(1.0 ppm\) -> Pelagic Predatory Fish / Cats / Humans \(20 to) Tj
T*
(   50 ppm in flesh, a 500,000-fold bio-concentration\).) Tj
T*
(   - Neurological Pathology: Methylmercury forms a covalent complex with L-cysteine, structurally) Tj
T*
(   mimicking the essential amino acid methionine. It readily crosses the blood-brain barrier via) Tj
T*
(   the LAT1 amino acid transporter, concentrating in the cerebral cortex and cerebellum, causing) Tj
T*
(   irreversible ataxia, paresthesia, blindness, congenital microcephaly, and death.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
