(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the role of Forest Ecosystems in global carbon dynamics, and evaluate the United Nations REDD+ framework for climate mitigation.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Forest Carbon Stocks, Deforestation Kinetics, and the UN REDD+ Policy Framework:) Tj
T*
(   1. Carbon Stocks in Forest Ecosystems:) Tj
T*
(   Global forests cover approximately 4.06 billion hectares \(~31% of Earth's land surface\) and) Tj
T*
(   store ~861 Gt of carbon, partitioned into distinct pools:) Tj
T*
(   - Aboveground Biomass \(AGB\): Living stems, bark, branches, and foliage \(stores ~44% of total) Tj
T*
(   forest carbon\).) Tj
T*
(   - Belowground Biomass \(BGB\): Living coarse and fine tree root systems \(~9% of carbon\).) Tj
T*
(   - Dead Wood & Litter: Coarse woody debris and fallen senescent leaves \(~11% of carbon\).) Tj
T*
(   - Soil Organic Carbon \(SOC\): Humus stored in mineral soil down to 1 m depth \(~44% in boreal and) Tj
T*
(   temperate forests\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Carbon Fluxes and Deforestation Impacts:) Tj
T*
(   - Mature tropical forests sequester ~1 to 2 Mg C/ha/year as Net Ecosystem Production \(NEP\).) Tj
T*
