(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the ecological and biogeochemical impacts of the Green Revolution, including pesticide bioaccumulation and synthetic fertilizer leaching.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Biogeochemical and Ecological Consequences of the Green Revolution:) Tj
T*
(   1. Technological Foundations of the Green Revolution:) Tj
T*
(   Initiated in the 1960s by Norman Borlaug, the Green Revolution achieved massive agricultural) Tj
T*
(   yield increases through three synergistic inputs:) Tj
T*
(   - High-Yielding Varieties \(HYVs\): Semi-dwarf wheat and rice varieties with high harvest) Tj
T*
(   indices.) Tj
T*
(   - Intensive Chemical Inputs: Synthetic Haber-Bosch nitrogen and organophosphate pesticides.) Tj
T*
(   - Mechanized Deep Well Groundwater Irrigation.) Tj
T*
(   2. Biogeochemical Perturbations:) Tj
T*
(   - Synthetic Nitrogen Leaching: Crop plants assimilate only 30% to 50% of applied chemical) Tj
T*
(   nitrogen fertilizers \(Nitrogen Use Efficiency NUE ~ 40%\). The excess dissolves as nitrate) Tj
T*
(   \(NO3-\), leaching through porous soils into rural groundwater aquifers. Nitrate levels exceeding) Tj
T*
(   the WHO drinking water limit \(50 mg/L NO3- or 10 mg/L NO3-N\) induce Infant Methemoglobinemia) Tj
T*
(   \('Blue Baby Syndrome'\), where nitrite oxidizes hemoglobin iron \(Fe2+ to Fe3+\), preventing) Tj
T*
(   oxygen transport.) Tj
T*
(   - Soil Acidification: Nitrification of excess ammonium fertilizers releases hydrogen ions:) Tj
T*
(   NH4+ + 2 O2 -> NO2- + 2 H+ + H2O, stripping essential basic cations \(Ca2+, Mg2+\) and causing) Tj
T*
(   chronic base depletion.) Tj
T*
(   3. Pesticide Resistance and Ecological Biomagnification:) Tj
T*
(   - Organochlorines \(DDT, Dieldrin\) and organophosphates \(Chlorpyrifos, Malathion\) eliminate) Tj
T*
(   broad-spectrum beneficial pollinator insects and natural predators.) Tj
T*
(   - Continued pesticide application creates strong selection pressure, driving the evolution of) Tj
T*
(   'Superweeds' and pesticide-resistant insect populations.) Tj
T*
(   - Hydrophobic pesticides accumulate in fatty tissues, leading to top-predator bird eggshell) Tj
T*
(   thinning and ecosystem collapse.) Tj
T*
