(   [Problem Statement]: Compare open raceway high-rate algal ponds \(HRAP\) with closed photobioreactors \(PBR\) for microalgae cultivation in biofuel production.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Microalgae Biofuel Cultivation Engineering: Open Raceway Ponds vs. Closed Photobioreactors:) Tj
T*
(   1. Microalgal Biomass Energetics:) Tj
T*
(   Microalgae \(e.g., Chlorella vulgaris, Nannochloropsis, Scenedesmus\) accumulate 20% to 60% of) Tj
T*
(   their dry cell weight as neutral triacylglycerol \(TAG\) lipids suitable for transesterification) Tj
T*
(   into biodiesel. They exhibit solar energy conversion efficiencies of 3-5%, far exceeding) Tj
T*
(   terrestrial oil crops \(oil yield: 5,000 to 20,000 L/ha/yr vs. 500 L/ha for soybean\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Open Raceway High-Rate Algal Ponds \(HRAP\):) Tj
T*
(   - Design: Shallow \(0.2 to 0.3 m depth\) oval looped raceway channels lined with geomembranes.) Tj
T*
(   Water circulation \(0.2 to 0.3 m/s\) is driven by a motor-driven paddlewheel to prevent algal) Tj
T*
(   settling and ensure uniform solar exposure.) Tj
T*
(   - Advantages: Low capital construction cost, low operational energy consumption, easy) Tj
T*
(   maintenance, and scalable across tens of hectares.) Tj
T*
(   - Limitations: Massive evaporative water losses, vulnerable to biological contamination) Tj
T*
(   \(predatory protozoa, rotifers, weed algae\), poor light utilization efficiency, and fluctuating) Tj
T*
(   ambient weather dependencies.) Tj
T*
(   3. Closed Photobioreactors \(PBRs\):) Tj
T*
(   - Design: Enclosed transparent borosilicate glass or polymer systems configured as Tubular) Tj
T*
(   loops, Flat-Plate panels, or Vertical Column airlifts. Filtered CO2-enriched gas is sparged) Tj
T*
