T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Mangrove Ecosystem Ecology, Coastal Hydrodynamics, and Blue Carbon Sequestration:) Tj
T*
(   1. Morphological and Physiological Halophytic Adaptations:) Tj
T*
(   Mangroves \(Rhizophora, Avicennia, Sonneratia\) are specialized halophytic woody trees inhabiting) Tj
T*
(   tropical and subtropical intertidal estuaries:) Tj
T*
(   - Stilt Roots and Prop Roots \(Rhizophora\): Extensive arching adventitious prop roots extending) Tj
T*
(   from the trunk, forming an interconnected structural lattice anchored in unstable coastal mud.) Tj
T*
(   - Pneumatophores \(Avicennia\): Vertical pencil-like aerial breathing roots emerging from) Tj
T*
(   subterranean horizontal cables, covered with lenticels containing aerenchyma tissue to) Tj
T*
(   transport oxygen into anoxic mud.) Tj
T*
(   - Salt Ultrafiltration: Root cell membranes selectively exclude 95% to 99% of NaCl through) Tj
T*
